  design_docs/mere_docs/implementation_strategy/2026-08-23_runtime_composition_acceptance_plan.md

That is a conatus crate split -- voxel extracted to its own crate, world.rs
rewritten around a rapier backend -- authored by a concurrent session, not by
the standards-survey work the subject describes. Anyone bisecting or reading
`git log --oneline` for the conatus split will not find it under a subject
that mentions it; it is here.

Cause, recorded so it is not repeated: a first commit attempt failed on
.git/index.lock while the other session was staging. The `git add` had already
run. On retry, a pathspec-less `git commit` took the whole index, which by then
held their staged work. The working tree was checked before committing; the
index was not. The fix is to commit with an explicit pathspec and to read
`git diff --cached --numstat` immediately before committing, not only
`git status` beforehand.

Left bundled deliberately, per the workspace rule against history surgery to
un-bundle a commit. Ruled by Mark 2026-08-24.
